-- title:
--   Triviality of χ∘ r on higher units at q
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field, Galois over $\mathbb{Q}$ with abelian Galois group, whose degree $[F:\mathbb{Q}]$ is prime. Let $\mathfrak f$ be an ideal of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb{Q}}$ that is an admissible modulus of degree $[F:\mathbb{Q}]$, i.e. $\mathfrak f \neq 0$ and, for every finite place $v$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ at which the chosen prime of $F$ above $v$ has nontrivial inertia subgroup in $\mathrm{Gal}(F/\mathbb{Q})$, the power $v^{\mathrm{admissibleExpOfDegree}\,\mathbb{Q}\,[F:\mathbb{Q}]\,v}$ divides $\mathfrak f$. Let $r$ be a homomorphism from the idele group of $\mathbb{Q}$ onto $\mathrm{Gal}(F/\mathbb{Q})$ whose kernel contains, and in fact equals, the subgroup generated by the principal ideles (the image of $\mathbb{Q}^\times$) together with the image of the idelic norm attached to the base change of adele rings along $\mathbb{Q}\to F$, and which satisfies the reciprocity formula $r(u)=\prod_{v}^{f}\mathrm{artinFrob}(v)^{\mathrm{ord}_v(u)}$ for every idele $u$ adjusted to $1$ modulo $\mathfrak f$ (congruent to $1$ to the prescribed order at each place dividing $\mathfrak f$ and positive at each real embedding). Let $\chi$ be an injective character $\mathrm{Gal}(F/\mathbb{Q})\to\mathbb{C}^\times$, let $\mathfrak q$ be a finite place of $\mathbb{Q}$ and let $m\ge 1$ satisfy $\mathrm{ord}_{p}(|d_F|)\le m$, where $p$ is the absolute norm of $\mathfrak q$. Then for every unit $u$ of the $\mathfrak q$-adic completion of $\mathbb{Q}$ with $|u|=1$ and $|u-1|\le \exp(-m)$, the local component at $\mathfrak q$ of the idele class character $\chi\circ r$, obtained by composing $\chi\circ r$ with the inclusion of the local units into the idele group, satisfies $(\chi\circ r)_{\mathfrak q}(u)=1$.
--
--   This is the bound 'conductor exponent at most discriminant exponent' for the reciprocity character $\chi\circ r$ of an abelian extension of prime degree: at each finite place the character is trivial on the higher unit group $U^{(m)}$ as soon as $m$ dominates the exponent of the residue characteristic in the discriminant of $F$. It feeds the construction of a finite-order Hecke character of $\mathbb{Q}$ with prescribed Euler coefficients and prescribed local triviality, used in the cubic-field input to the Langlands–Tunnell argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LanglandsTunnell_CubicLambda_localChar_comp_idelicArtinMap_eq_one_of_mem_higherUnitsAt_of_factorization_discr_le_of_prime_finrank.lean

